-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore): nouns for the "broadcasting apparatus" chain.
--
-- FORWARD-LOOKING ROW, TARGET unstable.  Not the answer of record.
-- The modules that use the time built-ins (`RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`, `EVAL UNDER VALID TIME`,
-- `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME`, TODAY) are read only by an unstable build; THIS module reads on any build.
-- See NOTES.md in this folder.
--
-- Nouns only: DECLARE and nothing else.  No rules, no #EVAL.
-- Membership test: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to this fact, or does answering it
-- require reading the Act?  Only the first kind is here.

IMPORT prelude

§ `Facts about one piece of apparatus`

-- A witness can say what an apparatus is capable of and what it is used for.
-- The first field is the first limb of the s 2(1) definition of "broadcasting apparatus".
-- The other three are the facts that the First Schedule's own definitions turn on:
--   "broadcast television receiver" means any apparatus used for the visual and aural reception ...
--   "broadcast sound receiver" means any apparatus used for the aural reception ...
--   "television receive-only satellite receiving system" means any apparatus ... capable of direct
--      reception ... from or through any communication or broadcast satellite in extra-terrestrial space.
-- (The first two definitions are in the three-item Schedule only; the substituted Schedule keeps the third.)
DECLARE Apparatus HAS
    `capable of or designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `capable of direct reception from a satellite in extra-terrestrial space`            IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Facts about what is transmitted`

-- The limbs of the s 2(1) definition of "broadcasting service".
DECLARE Transmission HAS
    `comprises a programme capable of being received, or received and displayed, as visual images`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `comprises a sound programme for reception`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `comprises a programme combining visual images and sound for reception or reception and display`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `is for persons having equipment appropriate for receiving it`                                  IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Facts about what a person does with the apparatus`

-- The three limbs of s 20(1), and whether the person acts under a licence.
-- Whether a licence was granted, and on what terms, is a fact about the licence; "holds a licence" is a plain input.
DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `operates it, or has it on premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `what is received on or by it`                                                              IS A Transmission
    `acts under and in accordance with a licence granted under section 20`                      IS A BOOLEAN

§ `The versions of the First Schedule`

-- Two texts of the First Schedule are in the sources.
-- The first has three items (broadcast television receiver; broadcast sound receiver; TVRO system).
-- The second, substituted by S 549/2012 and still in the Act, has one (the TVRO system).
DECLARE `Version of the First Schedule` IS ONE OF
    `the First Schedule of three items`
    `the First Schedule of the TVRO system only`

§ `The kinds of receiver a person has`

-- What a person says they have.  Each kind stands for the facts about the apparatus that the Act's words turn on:
--   television: used for the visual and aural reception of a broadcasting service (the Schedule's "broadcast
--               television receiver");
--   radio: used for the aural reception of a broadcasting service (the Schedule's "broadcast sound receiver", item 2
--               of the three-item text; AM and FM are not told apart by the Act, so they are not told apart here);
--   satellite dish: capable of direct reception from a satellite (the Schedule's "TVRO system").
-- All three can receive a broadcasting service.  The seat maps a kind to an `Apparatus` record in sgbau-seat.l4.
DECLARE `Kind of receiver` IS ONE OF
    television
    radio
    `satellite dish`
